<h1>Upload Status</h1>

<p>This page shows the progress of your benchmark upload. You will be automatically
redirected here after initiating an upload, or you can access it from your upload history.</p>

<h2>Status Information</h2>
<p>The page displays the following information about your upload:</p>
<ul>
<li><strong>Status</strong> - Current state of the upload (PENDING, PROCESSING, COMPLETED, or FAILED)</li>
<li><strong>Total files found</strong> - Number of benchmark files discovered in the archive</li>
<li><strong>Files processed</strong> - Number of files that have been validated and added to the database</li>
<li><strong>Directories scanned</strong> - Number of directories processed (for 'convert' method)</li>
<li><strong>Created at</strong> - Timestamp when the upload was initiated</li>
</ul>

<h2>Upload Methods</h2>
<p>StarExec supports two methods for uploading benchmarks:</p>

<h3>Convert</h3>
<p>The 'convert' method preserves your archive's directory structure. Each subdirectory
becomes a new space in StarExec, and benchmark files within those directories are placed
in the corresponding spaces. This is useful for organizing benchmarks into hierarchical
categories.</p>

<h3>Dump</h3>
<p>The 'dump' method discards the directory structure and places all benchmark files
directly into the target space. This is simpler and useful when you just want to add
benchmarks without creating a space hierarchy.</p>

<h2>Troubleshooting</h2>
<p>If your upload fails, check the error message for details. Common issues include:</p>
<ul>
<li>Invalid benchmark files that fail validation</li>
<li>Duplicate benchmark names in the target space</li>
<li>Insufficient permissions to add benchmarks to the target space</li>
</ul>

<p>After fixing the issue, you can try uploading again. Note that successfully uploaded
benchmarks will remain in the system even if a later upload fails.</p>
